### Notable Observation

The periodicity is **exact period-3**, not "approximately periodic" — the success probability hits exactly 100% at both k=1 and k=4, with exactly 25% at every other frame. This is because with M=2, N=8 the Grover rotation angle is θ = arcsin(√(2/8)) = 30°, and sin²((2k+1)·30°) cycles through values {sin²(30°)=0.25, sin²(90°)=1.0, sin²(150°)=0.25, sin²(210°)=0.25, sin²(270°)=1.0, sin²(330°)=0.25, sin²(390°)=0.25, ...}. The 25% values at k=0,2,3,5,6 are not "dips" — they're the random-guess baseline returning exactly, a consequence of the angle being a rational multiple of 180°.

